# ⚠ PII GUARD — THIS REPO IS PUBLIC. 2026-07-28: 29 untracked image/PDF artifacts were
# found sitting in the repo root, left over from the 2026-07-10 OCR band-measurement pass
# (blk_i*.jpg, pg*.jpg, block_*.png). Spot-checked blk_i9.jpg: a full DERM FOG eManifest
# showing five client names with street addresses, GDO permit numbers, the vehicle plate,
# the DERM decal number, the driver's name and signature, and the dump ticket number.
# They were never committed, but nothing stopped a `git add -A` from publishing them.
# Manifest/page images are ALWAYS client PII and must never be committed. Work on them in
# the scratchpad, not the repo. Do NOT narrow these globs to "just the known filenames" —
# the point is that the next ad-hoc pass gets caught too.
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
*.JPG
*.JPEG
*.PNG
# PDFs only at the repo ROOT (that is where the scratch lands). Deliberately NOT global:
# docs/audits/ and docs/reports/ hold intentionally-committed PDFs, and a global rule would
# shadow them. docs/reports/*.pdf already has its own rule above.
/*.pdf
# re-allow committed, non-PII product assets (add explicit exceptions here as needed)
!docs/**/*.png
!**/app-icon.png

# ⚠ PII GUARD, PART 2 — ROOT-LEVEL SCRATCH. THIS REPO IS PUBLIC.
# 2026-07-28: 61 untracked scratch files were swept out of the repo root (ad-hoc Management API
# query dumps: a1.json, o*.json, cli*.json, scratch_*.*, q*.json, dep.txt, and a stray `nul` from a
# `> nul` redirect). Several held LIVE CLIENT PII — addr.json and c174.json contained client names
# with street addresses. Nothing was ever committed, but only luck and the absence of a `git add -A`
# stood between those files and a public repo.
# Ad-hoc query output belongs in the session scratchpad, NOT in the repo. These globs are anchored
# with a leading slash so they only bite at the ROOT, where the scratch lands; docs/, scripts/ and
# supabase/ keep their own .json/.sql/.js normally.
/*.json
!/package.json
!/package-lock.json
/*.jsonl
/*.sql
/*.js
/*.txt
/*.csv
/*.log
/nul
# Backups live OUTSIDE this repo, in the workspace-level ..\backups\ (root CLAUDE.md §2). A
# backups/ folder had grown INSIDE the repo with 9 dump-test cleanup files; moved out 2026-07-28.
/backups/
